From 84cc59dc008a401e6af2bf004bb0069fdf981ea9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:33:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: the help of the internal disks says what the normal
 start does with the memory of devices

The normal start (the boot entries Run and Live) now also asks the kernel
for DMA translation: where the computer has an IOMMU, each device reaches
only the memory that the kernel maps for it. The entry that shows the
internal disks starts the kernel as LibreELEC does, every device with all
memory, and that cannot be changed once the system runs: the kernel takes
it from its command line only.

The help of "Show the internal disks (read-only)" listed what the normal start does
and this one does not (the lockdown); it now names the memory of devices
too. The help of the disks kept away said that the kernel runs with its
lockdown "as in the normal start"; it now says that, unlike the normal
start, devices are not kept to their memory, so a device whose firmware a
program has replaced could still reach the memory of the kernel.

English, and the Spanish of Spain, Argentina and Mexico.
